💭 A method that overrides another and keeps a parameter which the method it overrides
💭 only uses.
💭
💭 Expected: it compiles. The base method is marked 🎍🥡 on that parameter to say that an
💭 override may keep it.
💭 What happens: the compiler refuses the override: Function lets parameter "line"
💭 escape, which violates the overridden function’s promise. The mark on the base method
💭 changes nothing: what a method with a body does with a parameter is worked out from
💭 the body, and the mark is written over (MFFunctionAnalyser::popScope). That an
💭 override may not keep what its base only uses is meant: the compiler's own tests
💭 have such an override commented out. What is left is that the mark is taken and
💭 then ignored.
